&lt;h3&gt;


&lt;a href="https://orizens.com/blog/2026-06-18-zustand/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;When React Hooks Stop Scaling: Moving Complex State to Zustand&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a nice example of an architecture problem showing up as a bug. Oren Farhi explains how a speech recognition hook worked well at first, but became hard to reason about once transcript updates needed to come from outside the component tree&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Have you ever copied a Wi-Fi password, a code snippet, or meeting notes from your laptop to your phone?&lt;br&gt;
I used to email myself. Sometimes I sent messages to myself on WhatsApp. It worked, but it always felt slower than it should.&lt;br&gt;
So I built a simple solution.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F18e13wsbtjh1fsjbzl12.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F18e13wsbtjh1fsjbzl12.jpg" alt="ShareTextQR homepage showing the Generate QR Code button and key features" width="800" height="1422"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.tourl"&gt;sharetextqr.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Problem&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Moving text between devices is surprisingly annoying.&lt;br&gt;
Some common scenarios:&lt;br&gt;
Sharing a Wi-Fi password&lt;br&gt;
Sending code snippets&lt;br&gt;
Copying terminal commands&lt;br&gt;
Sharing meeting notes&lt;br&gt;
Classroom notes&lt;br&gt;
Event instructions&lt;br&gt;
Temporary passwords&lt;br&gt;
Most people use messaging apps or email.&lt;br&gt;
It works...&lt;br&gt;
But it's slower than it should be.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Idea&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Instead of sending text...&lt;br&gt;
Why not convert it into a QR code?&lt;br&gt;
Device A&lt;br&gt;
⬇️&lt;br&gt;
Paste text&lt;br&gt;
⬇️&lt;br&gt;
Generate QR&lt;br&gt;
⬇️&lt;br&gt;
Device B scans&lt;br&gt;
⬇️&lt;br&gt;
Done.&lt;br&gt;
That's it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real Use Cases&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
👨‍💻 Developers&lt;br&gt;
Share:&lt;br&gt;
Code snippets&lt;br&gt;
API keys (temporarily)&lt;br&gt;
Terminal commands&lt;br&gt;
JSON&lt;br&gt;
🎓 Students&lt;br&gt;
Share:&lt;br&gt;
Notes&lt;br&gt;
Assignments&lt;br&gt;
Questions&lt;br&gt;
Class materials&lt;br&gt;
🏢 Offices&lt;br&gt;
Share:&lt;br&gt;
Meeting notes&lt;br&gt;
Wi-Fi passwords&lt;br&gt;
Internal instructions&lt;br&gt;
Contact details&lt;br&gt;
🎉 Events&lt;br&gt;
Perfect for:&lt;br&gt;
Registration instructions&lt;br&gt;
Event schedules&lt;br&gt;
Booth information&lt;br&gt;
Announcements&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What I Learned While Building It&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
A good product doesn't always solve a huge problem.&lt;br&gt;
Sometimes it removes a tiny daily frustration.&lt;br&gt;
Those are often the products people end up using every day.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What's Next?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
I'm planning to add:&lt;br&gt;
Editable QR codes&lt;br&gt;
Analytics&lt;br&gt;
Custom QR designs&lt;br&gt;
Password-protected text&lt;br&gt;
Expiring QR codes&lt;br&gt;
Team sharing&lt;br&gt;
I'd love to hear what features you'd actually use.&lt;/p&gt;

